Description: control center for laptop keyboard lighting, fans and performance
 ByteKeys is a control center for Linux laptops, like the vendor apps on
 Windows (Armoury Crate, NitroSense, OMEN Gaming Hub). It controls the keyboard
 lighting (white backlights as well as single-zone, multi-zone and per-key RGB
 keyboards), performance modes, firmware fan curves and the battery charge
 limit, and detects the laptop and its keyboard automatically.
 .
 Features: live temperatures and fan speeds; performance modes synced with
 power-profiles-daemon; custom fan curves per mode (ASUS); full fan speed;
 battery charge limits; brightness, colors, zones and per-key colors;
 software and hardware effects; automations (dim on battery, off when idle,
 low battery and overheat warnings, Caps Lock indicator, schedules); profiles;
 the vendor launch key opens ByteKeys; a tray icon and a command line tool.
 .
 Hardware is reached through kernel drivers (asus-wmi, thinkpad_acpi,
 dell-laptop, system76_acpi, tuxedo-drivers and others), common USB lighting
 controllers, and OpenRGB. A small system service (bytekeysd) does the
 privileged work so the control center runs as a normal user.
